IMPORT prelude

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore) -- PART 3, PAYMENT OF SALARY, ss 20 to 33.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/EmA1968.txt
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No
-- pipeline, no independent test pass, no human gate.
--
-- WHAT THIS PART DOES. Three things: it fixes WHEN salary must be paid, it
-- computes salary for a month the employee did not work in full, and it says
-- what may be DEDUCTED and by how much. The deduction limits are the most
-- useful part, because they are the only place in the Act where an employee can
-- check an arithmetic answer against a payslip.
--
-- EVERY LIMIT IS SUBSTITUTABLE. "one-quarter (or such other proportion
-- prescribed in substitution by the Minister)" appears four times, and the 50%
-- cap in s 32 the same way. Each is carried as a supplied fact rather than as a
-- literal, so a prescribing order moves the answer and no rule needs rewriting.

§ `Employment Act 1968 -- Part 3, Payment of Salary`

§§ `The prescribed proportions`

-- The figures the Minister may substitute. Defaults are the Act's own.
DECLARE Proportions HAS
    -- s 29(1): deduction for damage or loss.
    `the damages deduction proportion of one month's wages` IS A NUMBER
    -- s 30(2): accommodation, amenity and service, per salary period.
    `the accommodation deduction proportion of the salary for the period` IS A NUMBER
    -- s 31(3) and (5): each instalment recovering an advance or a loan.
    `the instalment proportion of the salary for the period` IS A NUMBER
    -- s 32(1): the overall cap.
    `the overall deduction percentage` IS A NUMBER

`the proportions as the Act states them` MEANS Proportions WITH
    `the damages deduction proportion of one month's wages` IS 0.25
    `the accommodation deduction proportion of the salary for the period` IS 0.25
    `the instalment proportion of the salary for the period` IS 0.25
    `the overall deduction percentage` IS 0.5

§§ `20 -- Fixation of salary period`

-- s 20(1): the employer may fix salary periods. s 20(2): "A salary period MUST
-- NOT EXCEED ONE MONTH." s 20(3): "In the absence of a salary period so fixed,
-- the salary period is DEEMED TO BE ONE MONTH."
DECLARE SalaryPeriod HAS
    `a salary period has been fixed by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the fixed period, in months`                    IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the period` IS A SalaryPeriod
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fixed salary period contravenes section 20(2)` IF
        `the period`'s `a salary period has been fixed by the employer`
    AND `the period`'s `the fixed period, in months` GREATER THAN 1

-- s 20(3): the deeming.
GIVEN `the period` IS A SalaryPeriod
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the salary period, in months` IS
    IF   `the period`'s `a salary period has been fixed by the employer`
    THEN `the period`'s `the fixed period, in months`
    ELSE 1

§§ `20A -- Computation of salary for an incomplete month's work`

-- s 20A(1): where a monthly-rated employee has not completed a whole month
-- because they started after the first of the month, left before the end, took
-- unpaid leave, or took leave for national service under the Enlistment Act
-- 1970, the salary is:
--
--     monthly gross rate of pay
--     --------------------------------------  x  days actually worked
--     days the employee is required to work
--
-- s 20A(2): "any day on which an employee is required to work for 5 HOURS OR
-- LESS under his or her contract of service is regarded as HALF A DAY."
DECLARE IncompleteMonth HAS
    `the employee is monthly-rated`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `commenced employment after the first day of the month` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `employment was terminated before the end of the month` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `took leave of absence without pay for one or more days` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (c)
    `took leave of absence to perform national service under the Enlistment Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)
    `the monthly gross rate of pay`             IS A NUMBER
    `full days the employee is required to work in that month` IS A NUMBER
    `short days the employee is required to work in that month, of 5 hours or less` IS A NUMBER
    `full days actually worked`                 IS A NUMBER
    `short days actually worked, of 5 hours or less` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the month` IS AN IncompleteMonth
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 20A applies` IF
        `the month`'s `the employee is monthly-rated`
    AND `a reason in section 20A(1) applies` `the month`

GIVEN `the month` IS AN IncompleteMonth
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reason in section 20A(1) applies` IF
        `the month`'s `commenced employment after the first day of the month`
    ..  `the month`'s `employment was terminated before the end of the month`
    ..  `the month`'s `took leave of absence without pay for one or more days`
    OR  `the month`'s `took leave of absence to perform national service under the Enlistment Act 1970`

-- s 20A(2) applied to both sides of the fraction: a short day counts as a half.
GIVEN `the month` IS AN IncompleteMonth
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the days required to work, counting short days as half` IS
    `the month`'s `full days the employee is required to work in that month`
        PLUS (0.5 TIMES `the month`'s `short days the employee is required to work in that month, of 5 hours or less`)

GIVEN `the month` IS AN IncompleteMonth
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the days actually worked, counting short days as half` IS
    `the month`'s `full days actually worked`
        PLUS (0.5 TIMES `the month`'s `short days actually worked, of 5 hours or less`)

GIVEN `the month` IS AN IncompleteMonth
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the salary due for the incomplete month` IS
    (`the month`'s `the monthly gross rate of pay`
        DIVIDED BY `the days required to work, counting short days as half` `the month`)
    TIMES `the days actually worked, counting short days as half` `the month`

§§ `21 to 25 -- when salary must be paid`

-- s 21(1): ordinary salary, "before the expiry of the 7th day after the last day
-- of the salary period".
-- s 21(2): overtime, "not later than 14 days after the last day of the salary
-- period during which the overtime work was performed."
-- s 21(3): on completion of the contract, on completion.
-- s 22: on DISMISSAL, "on the day of dismissal or, if this is not possible,
-- within 3 days thereafter, not being a rest day or public holiday".
-- s 23(1): where the employee terminates WITH due notice or pays in lieu under
-- s 11, on the day of termination.
-- s 23(2): where the employee terminates WITHOUT notice, within 7 days.
--
-- Note the shape: the employer who dismisses has 3 days; the employee who walks
-- out gives the employer 7. The deadlines are stated as the number of days
-- after the trigger.
`the ordinary salary deadline in days after the end of the salary period` MEANS 7
`the overtime deadline in days after the end of the salary period` MEANS 14
`the deadline on dismissal in days` MEANS 3
`the deadline where the employee leaves without notice in days` MEANS 7
-- s 24(2): payment must not be delayed more than 30 days after notice to the
-- Comptroller of Income Tax.
`the maximum delay after notice to the Comptroller in days` MEANS 30

DECLARE PaymentOccasion IS ONE OF
    `ordinary salary for a salary period`
    `additional payment for overtime work`
    `completion of the contract of service`
    `dismissal by the employer`
    `termination by the employee with due notice or payment in lieu`
    `termination by the employee without notice`

GIVEN `the occasion` IS A PaymentOccasion
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the number of days allowed for payment` IS
    CONSIDER `the occasion`
    WHEN `ordinary salary for a salary period` THEN 7
    WHEN `additional payment for overtime work` THEN 14
    WHEN `completion of the contract of service` THEN 0
    WHEN `dismissal by the employer` THEN 3
    WHEN `termination by the employee with due notice or payment in lieu` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 7

GIVEN `the occasion` IS A PaymentOccasion, `the days taken to pay` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment was late` IF
    `the days taken to pay` GREATER THAN `the number of days allowed for payment` `the occasion`

-- s 25(1): payment must be made on a working day, during working hours, at the
-- place of work or another agreed place. s 25(2) disapplies that where salary
-- is paid into the employee's bank account in Singapore.
DECLARE PaymentManner HAS
    `paid into an account with a bank in Singapore in the employee's name or jointly` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid on a working day during working hours` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid at the place of work or another place agreed between employer and employee` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the manner` IS A PaymentManner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the manner of payment satisfies section 25` IF
        `the manner`'s `paid into an account with a bank in Singapore in the employee's name or jointly`
    OR  `the payment satisfies section 25(1)` `the manner`

GIVEN `the manner` IS A PaymentManner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment satisfies section 25(1)` IF
        `the manner`'s `paid on a working day during working hours`
    AND `the manner`'s `paid at the place of work or another place agreed between employer and employee`

§§ `26 and 27 -- what may be deducted at all`

-- s 26(1): "NO deduction is to be made by an employer from the salary of an
-- employee, UNLESS the deduction is authorised by or under any provision of
-- this Act or is required to be made" by a court order, a tax or premium
-- recovery declaration, or a direction of the Comptroller.
--
-- s 27(1) lists the authorised deductions, (a) to (k). (c) and (g) were
-- repealed.
DECLARE DeductionKind IS ONE OF
    `absence from work`                                     -- s 27(1)(a)
    `damage to or loss of goods or money entrusted`         -- s 27(1)(b)
    `house accommodation supplied by the employer`          -- s 27(1)(d)
    `amenities and services supplied by the employer`       -- s 27(1)(e)
    `recovery of an advance, loan, unearned employment benefit or overpayment` -- s 27(1)(f)
    `contributions under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953` -- s 27(1)(h)
    `any other deduction with the employee's written consent` -- s 27(1)(i)
    `payments to a registered cooperative society`          -- s 27(1)(j)
    `a prescribed deduction`                                -- s 27(1)(k)
    `required by a court order or a tax or premium recovery declaration` -- s 26(1)(a)-(e)
    `not authorised by the Act at all`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A DeductionKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deduction is authorised` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `not authorised by the Act at all` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 27(1)(d), (e), (i) and (j) each require the employee's WRITTEN CONSENT,
-- and s 27(1A) lets the employee withdraw it "at any time before the deduction
-- is made". s 27(1B): "An employee CANNOT BE PENALISED for withdrawing" it.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A DeductionKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deduction requires the employee's written consent` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `house accommodation supplied by the employer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `amenities and services supplied by the employer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other deduction with the employee's written consent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `payments to a registered cooperative society` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE Consent HAS
    `written consent was given`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `written notice of withdrawal was given before the deduction was made` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the consent` IS A Consent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consent stands at the time of the deduction` IF
        `the consent`'s `written consent was given`
    AND NOT `the consent`'s `written notice of withdrawal was given before the deduction was made`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A DeductionKind, `the consent` IS A Consent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deduction may lawfully be made` IF
        `the deduction is authorised` `the kind`
    AND `consent, where it is needed, stands` `the kind` `the consent`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A DeductionKind, `the consent` IS A Consent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `consent, where it is needed, stands` IF
        NOT `the deduction requires the employee's written consent` `the kind`
    OR  `the consent stands at the time of the deduction` `the consent`

§§ `28 to 31 -- how much may be deducted, head by head`

-- s 28(2): the deduction for absence "must not bear a larger proportion to the
-- salary payable at the gross rate of pay ... than the proportion the period
-- for which the employee was absent bears to the total period ... during which
-- the employee was required to work".
GIVEN `the salary for the period at the gross rate` IS A NUMBER
    , `the period for which the employee was absent` IS A NUMBER
    , `the total period the employee was required to work` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum deduction for absence` IS
    `the salary for the period at the gross rate`
        TIMES (`the period for which the employee was absent`
                   DIVIDED BY `the total period the employee was required to work`)

-- s 29(1): a deduction for damage or loss "must not exceed the amount of the
-- damages or loss caused ... and, EXCEPT WITH THE COMMISSIONER'S PERMISSION,
-- must not in any case exceed one-quarter ... of one month's wages and MUST NOT
-- BE MADE UNTIL THE EMPLOYEE HAS BEEN GIVEN AN OPPORTUNITY OF SHOWING CAUSE
-- against the deduction."
--
-- Three separate requirements: a ceiling at the actual loss, a ceiling at a
-- quarter of a month's wages which the Commissioner may lift, and a procedural
-- precondition which the Commissioner may not.
DECLARE DamagesDeduction HAS
    `the amount of the damages or loss caused by the employee's neglect or default` IS A NUMBER
    `one month's wages`                         IS A NUMBER
    `the amount the employer proposes to deduct` IS A NUMBER
    `the Commissioner has permitted a larger deduction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee has been given an opportunity of showing cause` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the deduction` IS A DamagesDeduction, `the proportions` IS A Proportions
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the quarter-of-a-month ceiling` IS
    `the deduction`'s `one month's wages`
        TIMES `the proportions`'s `the damages deduction proportion of one month's wages`

GIVEN `the deduction` IS A DamagesDeduction, `the proportions` IS A Proportions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the damages deduction is within the limits` IF
        `the deduction`'s `the amount the employer proposes to deduct`
            AT MOST `the deduction`'s `the amount of the damages or loss caused by the employee's neglect or default`
    AND `the proportionate ceiling is satisfied or lifted` `the deduction` `the proportions`

GIVEN `the deduction` IS A DamagesDeduction, `the proportions` IS A Proportions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proportionate ceiling is satisfied or lifted` IF
        `the deduction`'s `the Commissioner has permitted a larger deduction`
    OR  `the deduction`'s `the amount the employer proposes to deduct`
            AT MOST `the quarter-of-a-month ceiling` `the deduction` `the proportions`

-- The procedural precondition is separate and is not lifted by the
-- Commissioner's permission: "must not be made until the employee has been
-- given an opportunity of showing cause".
GIVEN `the deduction` IS A DamagesDeduction, `the proportions` IS A Proportions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the damages deduction may be made` IF
        `the damages deduction is within the limits` `the deduction` `the proportions`
    AND `the deduction`'s `the employee has been given an opportunity of showing cause`

-- s 30(2): a deduction for accommodation, amenity or service "must not exceed
-- an amount equivalent to the VALUE of the house accommodation, amenity or
-- service supplied", and the TOTAL of such deductions in any one salary period
-- "must not in any case exceed one-quarter ... of the salary payable to the
-- employee in respect of that period."
GIVEN `the total of such deductions in the period` IS A NUMBER
    , `the value of what was supplied` IS A NUMBER
    , `the salary payable for the period` IS A NUMBER
    , `the proportions` IS A Proportions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accommodation deductions are within section 30` IF
        `the total of such deductions in the period` AT MOST `the value of what was supplied`
    AND `the total of such deductions in the period`
            AT MOST (`the salary payable for the period`
                         TIMES `the proportions`'s `the accommodation deduction proportion of the salary for the period`)

-- s 31(2): an ADVANCE may be recovered "in instalments by deductions from
-- salary spread over NOT MORE THAN 12 MONTHS". s 31(3) and (5): an instalment,
-- whether for an advance or a loan, must not exceed a quarter of the salary due
-- for the salary period.
--
-- Note the asymmetry: the 12-month ceiling applies to ADVANCES only. s 31(4)
-- says loans "may be recovered in instalments by deductions from salary" with
-- no period limit at all.
GIVEN `the months over which the advance is spread` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the advance is spread within section 31(2)` IF
    `the months over which the advance is spread` AT MOST 12

GIVEN `the instalment` IS A NUMBER
    , `the salary due for the salary period` IS A NUMBER
    , `the proportions` IS A Proportions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instalment is within the limit` IF
    `the instalment` AT MOST (`the salary due for the salary period`
                                  TIMES `the proportions`'s `the instalment proportion of the salary for the period`)

§§ `32 -- the overall cap, and what escapes it`

-- s 32(1): "The total amount of ALL deductions made from an employee's salary
-- by an employer in any one salary period, OTHER THAN deductions under
-- section 27(1)(a), (f) or (j), must not exceed 50% ... of the salary payable to
-- the employee in respect of that period."
--
-- Three heads escape the cap: absence (a), recovery of advances, loans,
-- unearned benefits and overpayments (f), and payments to a cooperative
-- society (j). So an employee repaying a loan can be deducted more than half
-- their salary and s 32 has nothing to say about it; what limits that is
-- s 31(5)'s quarter per instalment.
--
-- s 32(2): the cap "does not apply to deductions made from the LAST salary due
-- to an employee on termination ... or on completion of his or her contract".
GIVEN `the kind` IS A DeductionKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deduction counts towards the section 32 cap` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `absence from work` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `recovery of an advance, loan, unearned employment benefit or overpayment` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `payments to a registered cooperative society` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the total of countable deductions in the period` IS A NUMBER
    , `the salary payable for the period` IS A NUMBER
    , `this is the last salary on termination or completion` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `the proportions` IS A Proportions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 32 cap is satisfied` IF
        `this is the last salary on termination or completion`
    OR  `the total of countable deductions in the period`
            AT MOST (`the salary payable for the period`
                         TIMES `the proportions`'s `the overall deduction percentage`)

§§ `33 -- priority of salary to other debts`

-- s 33(1): the section applies to -- (a) WORKMEN earning not more than $4,500 a
-- month excluding overtime, bonus, annual wage supplement, productivity
-- incentive and allowances; and (b) every EMPLOYEE other than a workman or a
-- person in a managerial or executive position earning not more than $2,600 a
-- month on the same exclusions. Both figures are substitutable by the Minister.
DECLARE Worker HAS
    `is a workman`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `is employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS A BOOLEAN
    `monthly salary excluding overtime, bonus, annual wage supplement, productivity incentive and allowances` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE SalaryCaps HAS
    `the workman cap`   IS A NUMBER
    `the employee cap`  IS A NUMBER

`the caps as the Act states them` MEANS SalaryCaps WITH
    `the workman cap` IS 4500
    `the employee cap` IS 2600

GIVEN `the worker` IS A Worker, `the caps` IS A SalaryCaps
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 33 applies to the worker` IF
        `section 33(1)(a) applies` `the worker` `the caps`
    OR  `section 33(1)(b) applies` `the worker` `the caps`

GIVEN `the worker` IS A Worker, `the caps` IS A SalaryCaps
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 33(1)(a) applies` IF
        `the worker`'s `is a workman`
    AND `the worker`'s `monthly salary excluding overtime, bonus, annual wage supplement, productivity incentive and allowances`
            AT MOST `the caps`'s `the workman cap`

GIVEN `the worker` IS A Worker, `the caps` IS A SalaryCaps
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 33(1)(b) applies` IF
        NOT `the worker`'s `is a workman`
    AND NOT `the worker`'s `is employed in a managerial or an executive position`
    AND `the worker`'s `monthly salary excluding overtime, bonus, annual wage supplement, productivity incentive and allowances`
            AT MOST `the caps`'s `the employee cap`
